title: '`pallet-accumulate-and-forward`: measure the transfer period from the last forward'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `on_idle` only forwarded when the block number of the configured `BlockNumberProvider` was an
    exact multiple of `TransferPeriod`. A chain that does not observe every block of its provider,
    e.g. a parachain using `RelaychainDataProvider`, can miss those blocks indefinitely.

    The pallet now records the block of the last forwarding attempt in the new `LastForwardBlock`
    storage item and forwards once `TransferPeriod` blocks have elapsed since then, whatever the
    block cadence. No migration is needed: an empty `LastForwardBlock` means "never forwarded", so
    after upgrade the first block with enough funds forwards immediately.

crates:
- name: pallet-accumulate-and-forward
  bump: minor
- name: emulated-integration-tests-common
  bump: major
  validate: false
